From af6fdd3451baaac6b2dd1df0d642aff941c733fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nassos Yiannopoulos <nassosyian@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:09:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 71/72] hw/display/pvg: complete command buffers early when the
 guest cannot see the results

Every submission waited for its fence before the stamp was published. Now
the executor records into two frames (command buffers, fences, arena
halves, retired-image lists), and render passes without write-backs and
compute dispatches without outputs return right after submission: their
GPU work only touches executor-owned memory. If they gather from guest RAM,
they wait just for the gathers (a separate submission) so the guest may
reuse its memory. With early completion, uploads up to 1 MiB are CPU
writes through resizable BAR (no gather to wait for). Guest-visible writes
(scatters, CPU write-backs), captures and dumps still wait. Object
deletion waits only when a pipeline or sampler is destroyed.

Property early-complete (default on; off with async). ~70% of command
buffers complete early; Mission Control executor ~200 -> ~180-196 ms per
500 cmdbufs, presents/s +5-15% (within run-to-run noise).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
